# Third layer: per-user, non-secret configuration.
#
# Parsed by `direnv dotenv` (KEY=value), NOT sourced as shell — no command
# substitution, no conditionals. Anything needing shell logic belongs in
# `.envrc.user` instead; anything secret belongs behind sops in
# `.envrc.secrets`.
#
# Unlike `.envrc.secrets`/`.envrc.user`, this file is deliberately NOT
# auto-created, because the strategies below are mutually exclusive and
# applying both at once would be wrong. Copy it and uncomment exactly one.

# Strategy A: keep shared on-disk config, override the active context per user.
# EXAMPLE_PROFILE=scratch
# EXAMPLE_ENDPOINT=https://example.invalid

# Strategy B: isolate this checkout's config and credentials on disk instead.
# EXAMPLE_CONFIG_DIR=/home/you/.config/example-envrcs-template
